* Developed with AI assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) -- 17 Nov 2026
* netrexx.pfx -- NetRexx definition for the prefix-macro framework
* (phase B).  Format as in rexx.pfx; shares src\pfxrexx.src with REXX.
* Source: NetRexx Language Reference (Cowlishaw and RexxLA; Version
* 5.10-BETA of March 4, 2026, in the 5.10-GA distribution): DO groups only (4.4), LOOP repeats (4.12), SELECT with CASE
* and an OTHERWISE that takes an instruction list without DO (4.22),
* CLASS, METHOD and PROPERTIES instructions (4.3, 4.13, 4.19); line
* comments -- and continuation by a trailing hyphen only (chapter 3).
* See BIBLIOGRAPHY.md.
*
* The macro is PFXNETREXX; the XEDIT file name is truncated to the CMS
* limit of 8 characters, PFXNETRE XEDIT.
§lang       NetRexx
§macro      PFXNETREXX
*
* Keyword case: the templates as written (ASIS); the user may ask for
* LOWER or UPPER (option <macro>_CASE / GLOBALV PFX_CASE).
§case       asis
§source     rexx
§unit       DO=3 IF=3 label=3 SELECT=1 WHEN=2
*
* Mask for the body lines the macro adds, as for REXX.
§mask       40:/* 70:*/ op:&placeholder
*
* Look-back: which lines don't govern indentation.  NetRexx continues a
* line only with a trailing hyphen, and has the line comment --.
§comment    /* */
§linecomment --
§continue   trailing -
§blank      skip
§label      colon label
*
* Indentation after the governing line's keyword: LOOP, CATCH, FINALLY,
* METHOD and PROPERTIES open a block as DO does.
§opens      DO=DO LOOP=DO CATCH=DO FINALLY=DO METHOD=DO PROPERTIES=DO ELSE=IF IF=IF SELECT=SELECT WHEN=WHEN OTHERWISE=WHEN
§nested     WHEN OTHERWISE
§dedent     WHEN=WHEN
*
* After a line starting with END (at the body's column), the insert
* aligns with the line the END closes (his original intent).
§closes     END
*
* METHOD and PROPERTIES are indented one DO unit from the nearest CLASS
* line above, not from the line above them.
§anchor     CLASS METHOD PROPERTIES
*
* Sanity check: PROPERTIES must precede the first METHOD in a class
* (Language Reference 4.19); refused, with nothing inserted.
§before     PROPERTIES METHOD
*
* ---- commands ----
§cmd        DO          §min 2  §desc Insert DO group
§first      do                                            §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end
*
§cmd        LOOP        §min 3  §desc Insert LOOP block
§var        -           §first loop forever               §cursor body
§var        FOR 2       §first loop for &placeholder      §cursor 9
§var        OVER 1      §first loop &placeholder over &placeholder §cursor 5
§var        UNTIL 1     §first loop until &placeholder    §cursor 11
§var        WHILE 1     §first loop while &placeholder    §cursor 11
§var        *           §first loop %op                   §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end
*
§cmd        IF          §min 2  §desc Insert IF
§first      if &placeholder then do                       §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
§row        text=else do
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
*
§cmd        SELECT      §min 3  §desc Insert SELECT block; SELECT CASE selects by the value of an expression
§var        -           §first select
§var        CASE 1      §first select case &placeholder  §cursor 12
§row        indent=SELECT text=when &placeholder then do  §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end
§row        indent=SELECT text=otherwise
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT text=end
*
§cmd        WHEN        §min 3  §desc Insert WHEN clause
§first      when &placeholder then do                     §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end
*
§cmd        OTHERWISE   §min 4  §desc Insert OTHERWISE clause
§first      otherwise                                     §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
*
§cmd        ITERATE     §min 4  §desc Insert ITERATE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      iterate                                       §cursor 8
*
§cmd        LEAVE       §min 3  §desc Insert LEAVE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      leave                                         §cursor 6
*
* ---- class structure ----
§cmd        CLASS       §min 3  §desc Insert CLASS instruction
§first      class &placeholder                            §cursor 6
*
§cmd        METHOD      §min 3  §desc Insert METHOD instruction and body
§first      method &placeholder                           §cursor 7
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
*
§cmd        PROPERTIES  §min 4  §desc Insert PROPERTIES instruction and body
§first      properties &placeholder                       §cursor 11
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
*
* Engine built-ins this language uses (no template): pending and case
* commands. Synonyms are the names the setup registers.
§builtin    .. CLINE RI RIC CLC CUC
§synonym    LOC=CLC UPC=CUC
